& [RequiredSurface]
  + introduce one safe-Rust effect-free component that accepts a complete sealed ProjectAssemblyResult plus one strict record identity
  + independently replay the supplied assembly envelope manifest generation and result seal before reading source bytes
  + recover an entire supplied SourceDocument or the exact declared SourceSpan for a kind context unit relation type relation rule or view
  + distinguish unknown record from known package without a source span and refuse malformed or non-boundary UTF-8 spans
  + return logical path source digest span digest exact text generation request digest result digest and explicit non-authority
  + make the result deterministic strictly serializable bounded and replay-verifiable
  + recognize capability kernel.sop.source-excerpt without admitting the whole cantor_scribe candidate

& [Acceptance]
  + Unicode excerpts are byte-exact and span digests bind the returned bytes
  + source-document requests return the complete supplied document
  + tampered assembly request result source text span path and digest states refuse
  + unknown package source-less record invalid identity unknown record oversized machine form duplicate field and trailing JSON refuse
  + focused debug overflow-checked release workspace warnings-denied Clippy format dual-host source and evidence replay pass

& [NonAuthority]
  + logical paths are attribution labels only and never authorize host path access
  + no filesystem read or write SQLite persistence index search ranking neighborhood completion evaluation reference graph authoring LSP MCP provider model process installation update remote machine merge publication or external effect
  + no byte from C:\Project\Cantor is modified staged normalized copied back or deleted
